  "notes": "Redeployed 24 October 2026 after the C-19 fix (non-reveal penalty timing bypass): the auction WASM changed, so the factory/registry (which pin its hash at construction) and the oracle adapter (which pins the registry) all needed a fresh, mutually-verified deployment rather than an upgrade. The OracleAdapter's `base` constructor argument is the quote/settlement asset (here CUSD), matching SEP-40 semantics where `lastprice(OracleAsset::Stellar(rwa))` reports the rwa's price denominated in that fixed base; an initial deploy with base=CRWA was a mistake, left unused and superseded by CDFIP6XT4RBKQHHOZQ6T3OUMM7AWYNST6IEKPVTLB3RMIV2EOU6RRY6M (recorded above). The original asset setup funded each user with 50 whole CRWA and 50 whole CUSD (500,000,000 raw units of each); later auctions change those balances, so current holdings must be queried on-chain. CRWA requires per-holder SAC set_authorized (already granted to all 10 users) and will be needed again for each new Auction escrow instance before funding.",
